# Template for .sanitize-denylist.local — copy this file to that name and fill it in.
#
# This file (the .example version) is tracked in git and must never contain a real
# value. The copy without ".example" is covered by the repo's "*.local" gitignore
# rule and is read at runtime by scripts/sanitize-check.sh (rule R5). The script
# treats a missing .sanitize-denylist.local as a hard error, not a skip, because
# an empty denylist would make the gate look like it passed when it never actually
# checked for the values that matter most.
#
# Format: one regex per line, extended regular expression (ERE) syntax, matched
# case-sensitively against every line of every scanned JSON file. Blank lines and
# lines starting with # are ignored — comment freely.
#
# What belongs in the real file:
#   - The real n8n instance hostname or IP, escaped for regex (dots are "."
#     metacharacters, escape them with a backslash).
#   - The real production server IPv4 address, same escaping.
#   - Any real project or client name that must never appear in an exported
#     workflow, even inside a credential name, a note, or pinned sample data.
#
# Examples of the *shape* these lines take (do not uncomment — replace with the
# real values in the actual .sanitize-denylist.local file):
#
# your-n8n-hostname\.example\.tld
# 203\.0\.113\.\d+
# any real project or client name
